algorithms.pseudocode:
INPUT  finite set S of positive loop lengths
OUTPUT relation R on {0,...,B}, B = max(S), with return set at 0 equal to <S>
1  B <- max(S)  (B <- 0 if S is empty)
2  R(i) <- empty set for i = 0..B
3  for i = 1 to B do R(i) <- {i-1}         // deterministic countdown
4  for each s in S do R(0) <- R(0) union {s-1}   // nondeterministic loop entry
5  return R
// correctness: jump to s-1 then descend = a return of length exactly s;
// every return decomposes as one such loop followed by a shorter return.
